  "knowledgePattern": "Combine conjugate radical fractions before solving on the original domain",
  "knowledgeTags": [
    "algebra"
  ],
  "solution": "<p>For real square roots and defined fractions, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02260;</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow></math>. The common denominator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. Multiplying by the nonzero denominator gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>132</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>108</mn></mrow></math>, hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>This satisfies the original domain, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>36</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></math>. Answer H.</p>",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Combine the fractions",
      "body": "<p>Use one common denominator, retaining the restrictions that make both original fractions defined.</p>",
      "recap": "Subtracting fractions requires a common denominator and brackets around a whole numerator.",
      "pitfall": "A minus sign outside a bracket applies to every term.",
      "pause": "Write the combined fraction without solving yet.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-extra-algebraic-fraction-operations",
          "reminder": "Subtracting fractions requires a common denominator and brackets around a whole numerator."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Use the conjugate product",
      "body": "<p>In the denominator, apply <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "For a real nonnegative input, squaring its principal square root returns that input.",
      "pitfall": "Do not confuse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Simplify the numerator and denominator, solve, and check the original restrictions.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l05",
          "reminder": "For a real nonnegative input, squaring its principal square root returns that input."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
